{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1227771-can-a-circle-of-dynasts-win","id":1227771,"title":"Can a circle of dynasts \"win?\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-15T15:31:11-07:00","id":1227771,"title":"Can a circle of dynasts \"win?\"","content":"<br /> Of course, the title of the thread is meant to be a bit provocative <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Let us imagine, arguendo, that a classic sort of conclusion to a dynast campaign is to put one of the PC's on the throne, the rest of the circle as the most powerful dynasts in the Realm, and to reform the Realm into the greatest civilization on the face of Creation, a beacon of justice and virtue that protects Creation from those things that would threaten it.<br /> <br /> The question, then, is this: is that even a plausible goal for a group of terrestrial dynasts in 3E?<br /> <br /> Allow me to play devil's advocate and answer in the negative:<ul><li>Terrestrial exalts are individually quite weak in comparison to all of the other powers in Creation; they simply lack the metaphysical power to overcome the obstacles.</li> <li>The Realm is a baby-eating rape machine of aristocratic decadence coupled with engineered (for Reasons) incompetent dysfunction and a myopic focus on short-term self-interest (when pursuing short-term self-interest is not reasonably calculated to achieve long-term success).</li> <li>The Realm is being smacked around by Lunars, secretly manipulated by Sidereals, and any newly-exalted Solar can punch even the most powerful dragon-blooded elder in half without breaking a sweat.</li> <li>Etc.</li> </ul>Now, I don't really want to debate the merits of my devil's advocate argument; these views are not consistent with the forum orthodoxy, and I don't want to generate a thread that simply reiterates that orthodoxy. Further, a YCMV argument may work for some people, but it's both an uninteresting response and an unsatisfying one from the perspective of a game that includes both rules and fluff (both of which I quite like).<br /> <br /> So, can a circle of dynasts win, or are they helpless in the face of more powerful actors in Creation with their own designs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T15:38:05-07:00","id":1227773,"title":"","content":"Let us imagine, arguendo, that a classic sort of conclusion to a dynast campaign is to put one of the PC's on the throne, the rest of the circle as the most powerful dynasts in the Realm, and to reform the Realm into the greatest civilization on the face of Creation, a beacon of justice and virtue that protects Creation from those things that would threaten it.<br /> <br /> I think, tbh, that the first is very achievable in game (my group did it... I only ended up as ambassador to Autocthon, but other PCs became Empress, Prime Minister, Head of the All-Seeing Eye, etc) though probably not in a short game.<br /> <br /> The second part, reforming into a beacon of justice...<br /> Well, reform, cultural and economic changes take time. A lot of time. And you're probably not going to be able to do it until after winning a civil war against reactionaries and counter-revolutionaries anyway.<br /> So, I don't really see it as viable in the short or medium-term. The long-term though? Yeah, it's possible. In fact, making it a beacon of justice and virtue probably makes protecting Creation much easier, because you may not have to fight Lunars and Solars quite so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T16:24:33-07:00","id":1227781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1227771-can-a-circle-of-dynasts-win#post1227771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, can a circle of dynasts win, or are they helpless in the face of more powerful actors in Creation with their own designs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that any answers we provide you are subjective, and amount to little more then personal opinions. That said, my opinion is that; yes Dynasts can &quot;win&quot; at least in part. Terrestrial PCs can absolutely win the throne. With that accomplished, they could definitely set about reforming the Empire into something a more efficient (though as the Wizard above said, this takes quite a bit of time to accomplish). They can, and should, use the Realm's military might to protect Creation from those that would see it destroyed! So the answer to your question is &quot;yes,&quot; a circle of Dynasts can win in this regard.<br /> <br /> However, I do not believe Dragonbloods have the power to save Creation. One of the big themes of Creation's current timeline is that it's slowly dying. The number of Shadowlands appearing and/or growing in Creation continues to rise. The number of Wyld-tainted lands and those completely reclaimed by the Wyld along the borders continue to rise. Enemies that want to see Creation destroyed or transformed into something else, have been gained considerable strength. Personally, I don't believe the Dragonbloods have the strength to turn it around at this point. They've passed the metaphorical point of no return for terrestrial powers to stop it. This doesn't mean though that Dragonbloods aren't integral to &quot;fixing&quot; Creation. Not even the Solar's have the power to be everywhere and do everything. Dragonbloods are vital to Creation's safety and well-being, but I believe they're going to need considerable help to pull Creation back from it's downward spiral!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T17:20:59-07:00","id":1227784,"title":"","content":"Pretty much any major win that the PCs get will be in some way facilitated by the Storyteller. Solars just have built in excuses for being the only person who could talk Ma-Ha-Suchi down, being the Mask of Winters' personal kryptonite or the one who finds the Five Metal Shrike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T23:24:51-07:00","id":1227819,"title":"","content":"If you choose to restrict the definition of winning to be ruling the world, then no. Those shining golden dudes are just too good at it for you to stop them, and given how things have been going without them its questionable if it would be good idea even if you could.<br /> <br /> That doesn't seem all that usefull a definition of winning though. The whole appeal of DBs to me is that you're not pushed so hard towards ruling and conquering, and it's really a bit more like a traditional fantasy RPG. (Not like dungeon-crawling traditional, but you're not automatically in conflict with the whole world and you're usually not your own boss.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T23:47:39-07:00","id":1227825,"title":"","content":"You might think that DBs are weak - but a DB who has mastered a celestial dragon style is a POWERFUL warrior.<br /> <br /> (ok I'm drawing on 2.5 experiences here, but still)<br /> <br /> like celestial water dragon style has an essence-stealing charm that can drain even a solar in but two or three blows...<br /> <br /> If a DB can get to essence 4, it can access charms that will make it a very serious opponent to anyone - even in social combat.<br /> <br /> The trick about DBs is that you have to make them work together. Make one set up an opponent, then have one deliver the final blow. It requires some thinking, but its not difficult","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T01:41:54-07:00","id":1227828,"title":"","content":"I'll split my answer:<br /> <br /> Thematically, well, yes. They'll have to be the most exceptional people in their society, and they'll have to eat the elephant one bite at a time to co-opt the rest of their society into social changes... but thematically yes.<br /> <br /> (Or at least, so I'd argue on grounds including allowing us to imagine a more open and diverse set of futures for the game setting, and play out the game as if it's high stakes and all of them are up for grabs. Other people would argue, and this was a common argument at least back in late 2e era and early 3e era that, thematically no, Dragonblooded can't do much to &quot;save the world&quot;, because &quot;It's the Solars' show&quot;, which is a reference to the idea that everyone has to be insufficient in order that the Solars can come to save the day, and on the grounds that Sidereal prophecy is otherwise undermined.).<br /> <br /> Now, mechanically, I wouldn't even begin to know how you'd answer that question. You certainly can't white room simulate it. The play rules don't really allow to abstract what the advantages are of masses of Dragonblooded against, say, 300 strong Lunar Exalted (or however many there are).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T02:30:39-07:00","id":1227830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1227771-can-a-circle-of-dynasts-win?p=1227819#post1227819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those shining golden dudes are just too good at it for you to stop them</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh. Most of them have been exalted about 2 years. There are literally thousands of Dragonblood who've been exalted over 100 years.<br /> <br /> There's only one group of Solars who have seriously managed to take on the Realm, and they were led by two of the only Solars to have been exalted for more than 5 years.<br /> <br /> Not to say that Solars aren't a serious threat, but if the Realm was united, they could do much better.<br /> <br /> Lunars are a much bigger threat, and one the Realm's had great difficulty with. But they're not impossible to beat.<br /> <br /> Or, of course, since we're talking about reforming the Realm... some kind of peace deal? That seems like a better idea than constant war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T03:18:54-07:00","id":1227834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1227771-can-a-circle-of-dynasts-win?p=1227830#post1227830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh. Most of them have been exalted about 2 years. There are literally thousands of Dragonblood who've been exalted over 100 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should maybe have specified long-term. They can probably keep them in check for a while, decades possibly, but eventually more and more will survive out beyond the realms reach and start building power bases.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1227771-can-a-circle-of-dynasts-win?p=1227830#post1227830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, of course, since we're talking about reforming the Realm... some kind of peace deal? That seems like a better idea than constant war.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you make peace with solars you're going to start making deals and negotiating with solars, which means eventually you're going to end up ruled by solars. They have too much to offer and are too good at negotiating to not bargain their way into being your boss.<br /> <br /> Which is really what kind of dooms DB or Lunar rule in creation, not that they can't put up a fight against solars but that solars being in charge works just too damn well for them to not eventually just wear you down to accepting their glorious rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T04:22:11-07:00","id":1227840,"title":"","content":"Once again I'd argue this is also a problem for a circle of Solars unless there's handwaving going on.<br /> <br /> Most chronicles are liable to rolling credits once one of the PCs is sitting in the Scarlet Empress' chair or some other equivalent gesture but the harsh reality of the situation is that there's an entire Solar Exalted host who don't necessarily want the same things as you. Are you going to restore the Solar Deliberative so you can be vastly outvoted by NPCs? Try to rule like a king over a group where &quot;I kneel to no one&quot; is probably a fairly common Principle.<br /> <br /> Good luck with that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T04:28:31-07:00","id":1227841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you make peace with solars you're going to start making deals and negotiating with solars, which means eventually you're going to end up ruled by solars. They have too much to offer and are too good at negotiating to not bargain their way into being your boss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh so <i> that's </i> why he stormed out of G7. Now it makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T04:45:03-07:00","id":1227842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1227771-can-a-circle-of-dynasts-win?p=1227840#post1227840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again I'd argue this is also a problem for a circle of Solars unless there's handwaving going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty fair.<br /> A small number of people taking power and making everything lovely for ever has never happened in Exalted... or really in real life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> there's an entire Solar Exalted host who don't necessarily want the same things as you. Are you going to restore the Solar Deliberative so you can be vastly outvoted by NPCs? Try to rule like a king over a group where &quot;I kneel to no one&quot; is probably a fairly common Principle. </div> </div> </div>In my experience, it's once they've seized power that Solar circles begin to turn against each other.<br /> <br /> When they're fighting to stop the Realm, they can put what seem like minor differences aside. But once you're in power, you find there's a million decisions that you disagree over, and they're all pretty important.<br /> <br /> Hey, my group can't even put our differences aside to stop the Realm. 3 Legions are on their way, and an Essence 5 Zenith+Eclipse+social Lunar couldn't stop the Dawn warlord and Solar-Sorcerer-Queen from going to war. They just have two many differences, and their countries, being right next to each other, are competing over too much resources and territory.<br /> <br /> Of course, it was suggested that they merge and one runs the war while the other runs the economy, but of course giant egos like Solars have will never trust each other like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you make peace with solars you're going to start making deals and negotiating with solars, which means eventually you're going to end up ruled by solars. They have too much to offer and are too good at negotiating to not bargain their way into being your boss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Eclipses. Nights*, Dawns and Twilights are not generally that good at it.<br /> <br /> *I play an Essence 5 Solar who was recently put in charge of chairing a peace summit. Shockingly, a Night Caste with loads of Craft, evocations, athletics charms and some melee and stealth charms was not actually be very good at chairing negotiations or ensuring peace and unity.<br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, tbh, in my experience Dragonblood and Lunars are better at negotiating than Solars. Solars have too much ego and arrogance. Solars are much better at intimidation though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T05:00:17-07:00","id":1227843,"title":"","content":"What do you mean by &quot;win?&quot; I feel that you're losing the thread of things by defining it as this sort of all-compassing eternal victory that nobody (with the <i>possible</i> exception of loyalist Abyssals) is capable of achieving.<br /> <br /> If you're playing a group of Dynasts, and you maneuver your families into positions of power, stabilize the Realm, beat back challenges from the prominent Anathema of the time and lead into an era of peace and prosperity under Dragon-Blooded rule, then you've won. Solars and Lunars will still be out there and may one day overthrow the new era of Dragon-Blooded hegemony you created; one day the Realm may fall. But not today.<br /> <br /> And that's... basically how it always is, regardless of who you're playing. With the possible exception of Abyssals, nobody ever gets to say that they won in the end, because <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/QpgRZrP.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">nothing ever ends</a>. If your goal for winning is &quot;achieve eternal victory forever in a way that can never be reversed by events in the future&quot;, you're dooming yourself to disappointment.<br /> <br /> (Even the most gonzo-crazy loyalist Abyssals just sort of have to take it on faith that there won't be another universe created after they destroy the current one.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 06-16-2018, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T08:05:26-07:00","id":1227854,"title":"","content":"The Empress &quot;Won&quot;. She beat the fair folk, set herself up as ruler of the dragonblooded and lorded over the civilized world as a tyrant for centuries.<br /> <br /> And now she's gone. And her empire is falling apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T08:30:50-07:00","id":1227856,"title":"","content":"It's a good point, it's not like this has never been done before... in the face of mass plague and a giant fae invasion.<br /> <br /> (Though the rest of her Hearth died...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T10:10:26-07:00","id":1227868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1227771-can-a-circle-of-dynasts-win?p=1227842#post1227842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars have too much ego and arrogance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars are exactly what you imagine them to be.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No, wait, that's ambiguous. Let me try again:<br /> <br /> \u200bSolars are an entirely fictional construct where, even within the context of their fiction, they're a distinctly unrealised element that is coming in unshaped by a prevailing trend, as goes their own personalities. Hence, their traits are what the one creating the universe and playing the characters would ascribe to them. As the default playable group, they are afforded a remarkable degree of carte blanche as regards the personality, motivations, goals and relationships of any given Solar.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt continuously amazes me that people don't seem to want to utilise this privilege, or are even aware of it. Between this and several other things, such as reading Alchemical Genesis womb Charms as though they mean that Autochthon has some weird hang-up about reproduction, or substituting how Ma-Ha-Suchi is actually written in the new core in favour of how he was written in Second Edition, and any other innumerable small things, I sometimes get an impression that many people only kind of half read the books. They come in with their own presuppositions on what they'll say with regards to the subject of powerful demigods (often shaped by what has been gleaned from hyperbole in Internet discussions), and just assume that the books conform to that.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo they miss out on things such as the varied personalities of the Solar signature characters*, and especially the Caste books, and the wide variety of characters that they present; not just varying degrees of arrogance and humility, of amorality and empathy, but just how much of an eclectic selection of amazing weirdos that they often are. It makes them small, and homogenous, and unflattering.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd then they attribute those boring people vastly disproportionate power and point it inerringly at the setting, ignorant of all of its diverse wonder and the potential therein, seeing the future of Creation only as a gold-tipped boot stamping on a human face over and over again, forever, with a face attached to the end of it shrieking &quot;conform, damn you&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe appeal eludes me.<br /> <br /> \u200b* Dace and Swan have too much ego and arrogance? Really?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T10:27:11-07:00","id":1227869,"title":"","content":"I feel it's probably important to refer to my whole sentence:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Me</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>In my experience</b>, Solars have too much arrogance and ego.</div> </div> </div> </div>And, indeed, the whole context, which was comparing them to Dragonblood and Lunars.<br /> <br /> In games I've played, Dragonblood and Lunars are better at negotiating, because Solar power discourages compromise; the lure of overpowering your opponents and thus being able to ignore clauses in negotiations you dislike is too tempting.<br /> Whereas Dragonblood, having been raised in an atmosphere of politics, and finding it less easy to just defeat all their foes and thus not need negotiation, are more likely to take it seriously.<br /> But of course, games I've played doesn't represent all Solars ever.<br /> <br /> This is not to say that all Solars are egotistical; just that I find them to be moreso than Dragonblood or Lunars (even when played by the same players). Nor am I saying they are<i> incredibly </i>egotistical and thus terrible at negotiation; I was just responding to the assertion that &quot;they're awesome at negotiation.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> I can't really deny your overall point, as I was making my own point about how varied Solars are in ability earlier, which is somewhat related to how varied their personalities and views are.<br /> <br /> Which, I think, feeds back to talking about the Realm negotiating with Solars. Some Solars may wish only to rule the Realm, and thus it's difficult to negotiate with them.<br /> Others may be keen on, say, protecting their own country, which could become a Realm ally. Or maybe they are devoted to fighting the Deathlords, and could be allies in that. Or maybe they just want to revolutionise agriculture or cure disease, and have no interest in politics, and so again could ally with the Realm (here's some resources, just keep improving agriculture).<br /> <br /> In short posts, I tend to overuse hyperbole!* Still, it makes for more of a debate than if I give nuanced longer explanations with caveats, I guess.<br /> <br /> <br /> *For example, when I said &quot;Solars are&quot; I meant as a general descriptor, an average or mean, rather than 100%. Like, say, &quot;people in Harbin are taller than people in Shenzhen.&quot; It doesn't mean 100% of them are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T10:31:36-07:00","id":1227871,"title":"","content":"The entire point of my post is that these are experiences that people create for themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T10:41:33-07:00","id":1227873,"title":"","content":"The Dragonblooded have &quot;won&quot; before.<br /> <br /> In the time before history, they waged war against the hosts of the Primordial and defeated them and made the world safe for humanity. A party of Dragonblooded PCs playing in this era would be running a war campaign with special ops missions assigned by Solars and Sidereals, with great epic battles and romances, trying to forge a world where their children can rule one day. That party of Dragonblooded PCs took down Celestial traitors, they defeated demon-god generals, they rescued captured Lunar spies and brought vital Intel that would change the course of the war back to HQ. They won, and ushered in an age of glory.<br /> <br /> When that age of glory was done, and the Solar tyrants had grown decadent and corrupt and mad in their gleaming golden citadels, another group of Dragonblooded PCs showed up. They saw the atrocities of their rulers and the grudging complicity of their houses, and they decided that risking death and dishonor was better than allowing such evil to stand unchallenged. They had help from a wise old man with stars in his eyes, and from a shapeshifting queen who had grown to fear and despise a man she had loved when the world was young, and from like-minded family members and old war buddies and a cute but surprisingly intelligent robot made of glittering blue ice. In secret, they built a rebellion, moved forces into place, desperately murdered to cover their tracks when some Night Caste got wind that something was up, sacrificed friends and lovers and like-minded rebels by acting loyal before the time was right... they gathered the secrets of their masters to turn them against one another, and when the time was right...they ruined a dinner party in the grand climax of the campaign. They saved the world, and ushered in a new Age! Their names would be remembered for thousands of years, and they would become legends and then religious icons in the retelling. They won! And they ushered in an age of freedom.<br /> <br /> When that age was done, a great darkness fell upon the land. Sickness laid waste to the world, and the hungry dead outnumbered the living. The shadowlands yawned wider, and at the edges of Creation a vast and alien host of nightmares and madness began to consume all things. In Creation's hour of need, a group of Dragonblooded PCs arose. They battled with warring factions of the disintegrating Shogunate, and with Balor's deadly assassins. They delved into ancient ruins and forbidden tomes and bargains with demons in search of cures for the world killing plague or weapons with which to defeat the Terrible Gaze! They had help, from a wizened Dragon King and an ancient Anathema's ghost and a mysterious old man who gave them hints and clues because they reminded him of some other brave young heroes he had known when the world was young. They braved traps and curses and the depths of Hell itself and in the end, at the climax of their campaign, they sacrificed themselves to save Ceation, giving a weapon that could defeat Balor into the hands of a brave and pragmatic redheaded NPC the ST hadn't even named because she was meant to just be a one off captain of some local troops but the whole party adopted her as PCs are wont to do. They won! They saved the world! They ushered in a seven hundred year empire!<br /> <br /> Anybody who thinks a party if Dragonblooded PCs can't save the world and ushered in a new Age doesn't get how Fate works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T11:05:33-07:00","id":1227875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1227771-can-a-circle-of-dynasts-win?p=1227873#post1227873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anybody who thinks a party if Dragonblooded PCs can't save the world and ushered in a new Age doesn't get how Fate works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T15:20:35-07:00","id":1227907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1227771-can-a-circle-of-dynasts-win?p=1227875#post1227875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, what?</div> </div> </div> </div>.. I use Fate in a &quot;how history was made and what parties of heroes getting together does to the setting&quot; sorta way here. Not a Loom thing, just a... destiny thing.<br /> <br /> Exalted PCs don't tend to lose, even if their victories aren't permanently or perfect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T15:33:26-07:00","id":1227910,"title":"","content":"I'd say you could make a plausible story out of it, but you'd need to have a Hearth of like, multiple heads of houses, or maybe one super powerful house or something I think. It's not plausible if you end it still at war with the Lunars AND the Solars though, you'd need some kind of setup where the Solars agree not to be in charge, but to still work with you. That'd be a hard sell, and you'd never convince a lot of them if they really didn't want it. It's not beyond the scope of reason that the majority of celestial exalted could be convinced that they screwed up the last time they were in charge, so they might settle for a cushy life where they get most of whatever they want but aren't in charge at the very top.<br /> <br /> Also if your Dynasts are like 20-30, I feel like that's stretching credulity, at least if you want your players to feel like they're driving the story. They're less respected, wealthy, old, and in all ways powerful than most of the other DBs in the Realm. They're much less numerous too. They're kind of cogs in the machine at that point, very important but ultimately small. Changing around a satrapy to be a good place might be more their speed.<br /> <br /> If you want to do more than that you're going to have to do what more classic RPGs and honestly stories in general do and give them an out. Give them an exhaust port on the Death Star, or a One Ring to destroy. It's not a bad thing, the rebel fleet is no match for the concentrated force of the imperial fleet, even Aragorn doesn't stand a snowball's chance in hell at facing off against a fully reincarnated Sauron, it's a pretty classic story which is really fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T18:54:07-07:00","id":1227930,"title":"","content":"Congratulations, the Empress-to-be as a group\u2019s pet NPC is my new favorite headcanon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T03:42:31-07:00","id":1227994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1227771-can-a-circle-of-dynasts-win?p=1227910#post1227910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say you could make a plausible story out of it, but you'd need to have a Hearth of like, multiple heads of houses, or maybe one super powerful house or something I think.</div> </div> </div> </div> Or individuals that those kind of people value and trust.<br /> <br /> Much as being &quot;the person this prominent NPC trusts&quot; is a PC cliche there is a reason why it exists. That kind of relationship draws attention away from the real reasons the PCs find tend to find themselves ultimately dominating the story, their inexplicable and effortless skill growth compared to pretty much everyone else in the world.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T04:27:10-07:00","id":1227999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1227771-can-a-circle-of-dynasts-win?p=1227910#post1227910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also if your Dynasts are like 20-30, I feel like that's stretching credulity, at least if you want your players to feel like they're driving the story. They're less respected, wealthy, old, and in all ways powerful than most of the other DBs in the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWealth and respect are things that you can take as 5-dot Merits at character creation.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd while Dynasts older than a hundred might be a dot or two higher than Essence 3, they're distinctly assumed to not be very numerous this time around.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo there's a question of whether an Exalt, particularly one whose powers have the kind of dependencies that the Dragon Blooded are bound to, can ever be outdone by a slightly less powerful Exalt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T06:16:08-07:00","id":1228019,"title":"","content":"Plus the game is built on the expectation that a PC deeb will be like essence 5 at 40 and trample over everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T08:46:43-07:00","id":1228046,"title":"","content":"I keep thinking of historical examples in which younger people came to power and made significant social overhauls and accumulated great authority for themselves.<br /> <br /> \u200bNow, in fairness, a number of these were instances of hereditary monarchy, but that doesn't necessarily mean that they were acting without constraint; still instances in which they might need to do things in defiance of regents or minsters or the general status quo of the conservative aristocracy.<br /> <br /> \u200bNot to mention instances of people coming from backgrounds that were not predisposed to significant power and authority getting into the game, and proving highly adept at it; swineherds who join the lowest ranks of the palace guard and become the new emperor, and the consorts of their sons who start out as seamstresses and become rather significant administrators and legislators.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd those not having the additional advantages that can be afforded by varying kinds of magic (which can be diverse in application in a manner that affords options even if the opposition has some that is stronger).<br /> <br /> \u200bOne should not constrain the construction of their settings or development of their characters by buying too heavily into narratives saying that the conservative status quo is something too entrenched to be overturned, or too advantaged to be outmaneuvered; not when they've been refuted on numerous occasions in reality. For any conceivable setting in which the player characters are limited by the idea that their elders know better, there's another in which one can approach from the idea that their elders know things that have become outdated, or at the very least are sufficiently set in their ways that there are possibilities that they do not see or will not consider.<br /> <br /> \u200bSure, the setup of the Realm is fairly effectively devised to cultivate conformity in each generation, but the Time of Tumult represents possibilities for significantly overturning the status quo in a manner that may be beyond the institutions of the Realm. One can play characters from a basis that their adventures in the Threshold in this time of significant change has them coming back to the Realm with ideas and inspiration for seeing it through to the Third Age that the hierarchy is incapable of considering.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat might not necessarily be something that helps them achieve power in and of itself, but I think it's worth considering.<br /> <br /> \u200bMind, depending on how one's story develops... Lea has pointed out how the Roseblack really makes more sense as a candidate for the Scarlet Throne when the Realm has been at war for a few years, a lot of the schemes of the old leadership have come to naught (and some of them dead alongside it), and her status as a charismatic, accomplished general might be the kind of thing that draws support simply because people want the fighting to end.<br /> <br /> \u200bImagine some substitutions for that which could be found through the process of characters who, amidst a Realm that is falling apart, advocate for an adjustment in how the Realm conducts itself in world affairs, and some alterations to the culture and lifestyle of the Dragon Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T09:47:24-07:00","id":1228059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1227771-can-a-circle-of-dynasts-win?p=1227869#post1227869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In games I've played, Dragonblood and Lunars are better at negotiating, because Solar power discourages compromise; the lure of overpowering your opponents and thus being able to ignore clauses in negotiations you dislike is too tempting.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's how it is, then me and my friends have been looking at and playing this game all wrong.<br /> <br /> In every single one of our games, (the ones where Solars are important anyways) the <i>one </i>reason Solars are able to threaten the Realm and change Creation in such amazing ways is because they're nigh-unmatched social monsters who can create massive empires overnight, turn entire villages and towns to their sides with awesome speeches and the like, and then train them into elite warriors, doctors and philosophers, creating high-intellect societies that have massive militaries that they can use to smash every other kingdom that isn't ruled by Solars into dust.<br /> <br /> We repeatedly emphasize that their social stuff (and crafting stuff, too) is their <i>most </i>powerful stuff by a mile- They can be adventurers and insane badasses individually- But in the end, the Sunny Boys are <i>built </i>to drag <i>legions</i> of people around with them. Solars can change the world because they can create great empires that they can use to gain resources, beat down their enemies and develop new tech and the like- Not because they can be the best swordsman ever.<br /> <br /> Without those social abilities, Solars in our game would just be another 150 dudes who are slightly stronger than Lunars- They wouldn't change a damn thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13269-particlestabilitybalance","name":"ParticleStabilityBalance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T10:54:54-07:00","id":1228069,"title":"","content":"How much of that is their actual willingness to compromise with other people though?<br /> Could you have achieved the same result as those awesome speeches with the social character instead simply shouting &quot;I'M SO PRETTY!&quot; or &quot;KNEEL BEFORE ZOD!&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T11:14:36-07:00","id":1228072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParticleStabilityBalance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1227771-can-a-circle-of-dynasts-win?p=1228059#post1228059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars can change the world because they can create great empires that they can use to gain resources, beat down their enemies and develop new tech and the like- Not because they can be the best swordsman ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have some issues with privileging one over the other.<br /> <br /> \u200bAt the same time as needing to find ways to reconcile the idea that Solars as warriors being an equally legitimate and useful part of their mythos with the issues inherent in violence as a method of solving problems.<br /> <br /> It's a balancing act, to be sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T12:31:45-07:00","id":1228094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1227771-can-a-circle-of-dynasts-win?p=1228069#post1228069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much of that is their actual willingness to compromise with other people though?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on your players- In the end, Exaltation doesn't give you a bigger ego, and it doesn't take away all of your flaws either. Solars aren't any more likely to be giant arrogant assholes than any other type of Exalted, (except maybe Infernals) even though they'll probably have an easier time of it. If your experience with Solars is that they tend to have big egos, then that's your group's fault. My group has more Solars who are humble (or simply aren't idiots) than they have Solars who can't compromise with others. And if a Solar is willing to compromise with other Exalts (And with other beings overall), then odds are he would be even more powerful than the the one who isn't.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1227771-can-a-circle-of-dynasts-win?p=1228069#post1228069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you have achieved the same result as those awesome speeches with the social character instead simply shouting &quot;I'M SO PRETTY!&quot; or &quot;KNEEL BEFORE ZOD!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Could we? Yeah, sure. We've done it before. Except you're going to have a real hard time make a working society just by being impossibly magically beautiful and only having people who are obsessed with your beauty and sexuality obeying you. For the &quot;KNEEL BEFORE ZOD!&quot; one, it also works, but it also means the people under you are going to obey you out of fear and because you dominated them forcefully. That makes it easy for you to be betrayed. Remember the Usurpation?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13269-particlestabilitybalance","user":"ParticleStabilityBalance","date":". 06-17-2018, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13269-particlestabilitybalance","name":"ParticleStabilityBalance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T15:32:48-07:00","id":1228133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1227771-can-a-circle-of-dynasts-win?p=1227994#post1227994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Or individuals that those kind of people value and trust.<br /> <br /> Much as being &quot;the person this prominent NPC trusts&quot; is a PC cliche there is a reason why it exists. That kind of relationship draws attention away from the real reasons the PCs find tend to find themselves ultimately dominating the story, their inexplicable and effortless skill growth compared to pretty much everyone else in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes that's very true, but you're not doing it the way that a Solar would do it. A Solar in a similar situation would experience a vastly quicker meteoric rise because there's no such thing as an empire of Solars above them that they need to contend with, and once they're at the top they can snag an audience with the rulers of whatever nation they're in and say &quot;Hey guys, I know you're mad but...Solar empire?&quot;*. Which is possible as DBs in the Realm, but you're probably getting the social version of the Death Star exhaust port to get there. There is some reason that the ST introduced to put the PCs in that position.<br /> <br /> <br /> *This in lieu of me writing a 5 paragraph 3 dot stunt speech for the sake of example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1227771-can-a-circle-of-dynasts-win?p=1227999#post1227999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bWealth and respect are things that you can take as 5-dot Merits at character creation.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd while Dynasts older than a hundred might be a dot or two higher than Essence 3, they're distinctly assumed to not be very numerous this time around.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo there's a question of whether an Exalt, particularly one whose powers have the kind of dependencies that the Dragon Blooded are bound to, can ever be outdone by a slightly less powerful Exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really a matter of if a DB can be outdone by a slightly less powerful DB, that's obviously true. The problem is that even if you spent all your BP on merits and took every social merit you could on chargen, that doesn't make you the head of a dynastic house. You are QUITE impressive, with connections all over the place, and in a lot of those cases those connections put you in a position of authority, but that doesn't make a thousand DB beholden to you, like Mnemon has. So you're not even as politically powerful as Mnemon, and you're going 12v1 in the political realm against every other house.<br /> <br /> Remember here, the original question was reforming the Realm, the REALM, into a &quot;beacon of justice and virtue&quot;. This isn't just as simple as ending slavery in the Realm, or maybe getting them to lay off the expansion and extraction gig they've got, as if that wouldn't be hard enough. This is about how plausible is it that you turn the whole realm completely upside-down on it's head all while the wolves of Celestial exalted are hammering down their gates, in an already toxic environment of fear and fierce tribalism.<br /> <br /> As a Solar, yeah that makes sense, you have unbridled power and force of personality that has not been seen in this world for a millennium or more, but as a DB you don't really have anything that those other people don't. Which again isn't to say it can't be done, you're just going to need some ST help with it to give you an avenue to do it. Like if they got a hold of the Imperial Manse, for example, that'd do it for sure. In contrast, for example, Solars don't need the ST to give them dick-diddly.<br /> <br /> It's not just social stuff, if you took a group of chargen DBs and pitted them up against Octavian, Siggereth and a legion of 500 blood apes, there's almost no way to win. Barring maybe some weird exploity white room thing like everyone taking 3 5-dot command merits and just drowning them in legions or something. Which isn't to say that the cause is hopeless either, you're just going to need some way to maybe separate them, like discover that Octavian has an ancient geas put on him by some anathema that prevents him from turning down an invitation to a summer fire festival or something. Or perhaps find some hellish intrigue that you can use to pit them against eachother.<br /> <br /> A Solar circle on the other hand just jumps in there and deals with the problem using the best solution, the Dawn solution.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *This in lieu of me writing a 5 paragraph 3 dot stunt speech for the sake of example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T16:50:12-07:00","id":1228146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1227771-can-a-circle-of-dynasts-win?p=1228046#post1228046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep thinking of historical examples in which younger people came to power and made significant social overhauls and accumulated great authority for themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in any rebuttal to this, but as a jump off point, these kind of ideas do point me to a question that this whole discussion makes me want to put out there in relation to the Realm: How would people on here handle a Realm Dragonblooded who was the equivalent of someone like Muhammad or Siddhartha or Master Kong?<br /> <br /> That is someone who pretty much came from a not particularly important social background, wasn't particularly old or experienced, but revolutionized the society in which they lived, though something like moral or religious genius or overwhelming charisma.<br /> <br /> Like, is that kind of person even possible as a Dragonblooded within the Dynasty and the mechanics as people think of it? Seems like they kind of should be.<br /> <br /> But on the other hand it kind of seems like there is ITT also the suggestion that the mechanics of the setting should preclude this kind of disruptive genius happening within Dragonblooded society and that elders will always be more socially powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T17:16:52-07:00","id":1228152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1227771-can-a-circle-of-dynasts-win?p=1228133#post1228133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you're not even as politically powerful as Mnemon, and you're going 12v1 in the political realm against every other house.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThere are approaches to the subject that are a bit more clever.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor example, promote and provoke conflict between all of the Houses in a manner that weakens them and discredits their leadership, while working to set oneself up as a worthwhile candidate for a position of significant authority as various ranks start to look for alternative solutions to the problem than coming under the leadership of the people that have led them into that mess.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlternatively, cultivate power outside of the Great Houses; the patricians, the magistrates, the outcastes, maybe even the peasantry. Create a banner under which they can pull together into a force of approximately equivalent strength to a Great House, that can compete on their playing field.<br /> <br /> \u200bHeh, there's something in there that I myself have never considered before; the idea of a Dynast (or several of them) renouncing their House name. Hell, in the absence of the Scarlet Empress, and as the credibility of the Realm's institutions breaks down, there's not exactly anything strictly preventing a collection of disillusioned Dragon Blooded from across the Realm breaking away, joining together, and declaring themselves to be a new Great House.<br /> <br /> \u200bOr, taking inspiration from the Japanese warring states, sections of the Immaculate Order that are dissatisfied with being involved in the struggles of the Scarlet Dynasty (probably a schism that fractures along lines that leave out a lot of Mnemon scions) organise themselves as a separate polity under which other unhappy elements of Realm society pull together and hold themselves apart, fighting to defend their sovereignty.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember here, the original question was reforming the Realm, the REALM, into a &quot;beacon of justice and virtue&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That can only ever come at the far end of a long journey. It makes no sense to consider development of that narrative and look at every possible first step with an attitude of &quot;this can't be done, because the current power structure won't allow it&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bA Dynast with a decent amount of mystical power combined with immense political capital and unfathomable riches may still be at a disadvantage, but I feel as though some people too often look at disadvantaged situations as something to resolve with head-on collisions that are liable to fail, rather than approaching problems sideways.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd when you've got cash and friends and respect, there are more sideways from which to approach than if you lacked those things.<br /> <br /> \u200bBesides, sure Mnemon has political power. The basis of that power is in things represented through the social system; use that system, in combination with the transformative circumstances of the Time of Tumult, to break the foundations of that power down.<br /> <br /> \u200bWould one look at the fact that Mnemon, or any other character, is still alive and has a backstory involving several instances of having gotten into brutal fights, and use that as an argument against actually engaging with her through the combat system? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">as a DB you don't really have anything that those other people don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>By this basis, how does anybody ever accomplish anything? Like, even within the context of evaluating the Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> \u200bPeople aren't interchangeable, and they're more than just their basic capabilities; they're their motivation, their circumstances, their relationships. All of these things mix together to create a unique instance that can generate unusual outcomes.<br /> <br /> \u200bMnemon has immense political power, and her son went down among the Mountain Folk, fought their enemies and earned their respect. He didn't do that on the strength of having powers that no other Dragon Blood had. If he had been motivated, do you not think that he could have utilised that respect to achieve some significant results? Possibly ones that would have been contrary to Mnemon?<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat about Mnemon herself? How did she survive Ragara's assassins when so many other siblings did not? Could just any Terrestrial have tamed V'neef's ancient monster wolf? Is Sesus Nagezzer not in a position to utilise his army of reprobates to accomplish some things of significance in the Realm?<br /> <br /> Look at the stories of the Dragon Blooded and try to find ways in which one's particular drive, what they are compelled to use their powers <i>for</i>, creates stories in which they can compete against their superiors.<br /> <br /> After all, that's the other way to utilise the point that other people don't have anything that you don't; 20-year old Mnemon didn't have any powers that you're not capable of, and look what she accomplished.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which again isn't to say it can't be done, you're just going to need some ST help with it to give you an avenue to do it. Like if they got a hold of the Imperial Manse, for example, that'd do it for sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWho cares about doing it for sure? Embrace unpredictability. Take risks. &quot;<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><i>Alea iacta est&quot;</i></span></span></div><br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not just social stuff, if you took a group of chargen DBs and pitted them up against Octavian, Siggereth and a legion of 500 blood apes, there's almost no way to win. Barring maybe some weird exploity white room thing like everyone taking 3 5-dot command merits and just drowning them in legions or something. Which isn't to say that the cause is hopeless either, you're just going to need some way to maybe separate them, like discover that Octavian has an ancient geas put on him by some anathema that prevents him from turning down an invitation to a summer fire festival or something. Or perhaps find some hellish intrigue that you can use to pit them against eachother.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bDoes that not sound like an interesting precipice to stand at the edge of?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T17:26:51-07:00","id":1228154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1227771-can-a-circle-of-dynasts-win?p=1228146#post1228146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not in any rebuttal to this, but as a jump off point, these kind of ideas do point me to a question that this whole discussion makes me want to put out there in relation to the Realm: How would people on here handle a Realm Dragonblooded who was the equivalent of someone like Muhammad or Siddhartha or Master Kong?<br /> <br /> That is someone who pretty much came from a not particularly important social background, wasn't particularly old or experienced, but revolutionized the society in which they lived, though something like moral or religious genius or overwhelming charisma.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWhile I wouldn't fully discount the significance of the personality of figures such as Muhammad, I wouldn't entirely attribute their success to them having something like a unique and overpowering force of personality. There have to have been social forces that were receptive to the message that he was preaching, and that were ready to start flowing when somebody with the right idea spoke up to give them a push.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhich speaks to another perspective on how one can approach the question of how a wealthy and influential Dynast might push back against Mnemon; the idea of seeking the support of elements of Realm society that are invisible to her, in ways of which she would not conceive. There's no systemic difference that would make the idea of rallying the support of peasants through things like actually looking for what they want out of the world and offering to accommodate it something that she would never consider, but it's still a difference in characterisation, in what results the mechanics are <i>applied</i> towards seeking, that generates different stories.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's like Lore backgrounds. The mechanics are only doing half of the job.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T00:27:04-07:00","id":1228222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParticleStabilityBalance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1227771-can-a-circle-of-dynasts-win?p=1228094#post1228094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends on your players- In the end, Exaltation doesn't give you a bigger ego, and it doesn't take away all of your flaws either. Solars aren't any more likely to be giant arrogant assholes than any other type of Exalted, (except maybe Infernals) even though they'll probably have an easier time of it. If your experience with Solars is that they tend to have big egos, then that's your group's fault. My group has more Solars who are humble (or simply aren't idiots) than they have Solars who can't compromise with others. And if a Solar is willing to compromise with other Exalts (And with other beings overall), then odds are he would be even more powerful than the the one who isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point was that your examples were more of Solars being good at influencing people, not necessarily cooperating with them. Convincing the town to follow you is actually really easy because on that level you're not dealing with fully fledged NPCs. The Storyteller can punish you for giving them a message with absolutely no substance but mileage will vary on that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1227771-can-a-circle-of-dynasts-win?p=1228133#post1228133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes that's very true, but you're not doing it the way that a Solar would do it. A Solar in a similar situation would experience a vastly quicker meteoric rise because there's no such thing as an empire of Solars above them that they need to contend with, and once they're at the top they can snag an audience with the rulers of whatever nation they're in and say &quot;Hey guys, I know you're mad but...Solar empire?&quot;*. Which is possible as DBs in the Realm, but you're probably getting the social version of the Death Star exhaust port to get there. There is some reason that the ST introduced to put the PCs in that position.</div> </div> </div> </div>My experience of this is that the narrative still generally lets a Solar PC 'cheat' in that the leadership of these other nations tends to be handled in much broader strokes than the Realm on the understanding that these people are ultimately unimportant to the overall story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T02:35:03-07:00","id":1228236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1227771-can-a-circle-of-dynasts-win?p=1228222#post1228222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point was that your examples were more of Solars being good at influencing people, not necessarily cooperating with them. </div> </div> </div> </div>This was what I was getting at. It's not that Solars are bad at social-fu, they're very good at it.<br /> But often having such power makes it too tempting not to co-operate with people, but instead bulldoze them with social-fu (or kung-fu).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I wouldn't fully discount the significance of the personality of figures such as Muhammad, I wouldn't entirely attribute their success to them having something like a unique and overpowering force of personality. There have to have been social forces that were receptive to the message that he was preaching, and that were ready to start flowing when somebody with the right idea spoke up to give them a push.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good point.<br /> And I think a lot of what allows Dragonblood PCs to rise to power in the canon game is that there <i>is </i>a specific time of flux. With a civil war in the offing, Anathema returning, etc, many DBs may be looking for something different and new. For example, without the Empress, do you just get a new Empress (Mnemon says yes, her, but many DBs would prefer something more cooperative), or do something new? With the appearance of the Deathlords, is fighting Lunars the priority? With the satrapies getting restless and troops being withdrawn from them, can it still carry out such an oppressive imperial policy?<br /> <br /> Also, related to that, &quot;great men&quot; are not just often the confluence of specific social changes, but also often the figureheads/representatives for a confluence of influence groups. Your PCs are not necessarily just 5 lone heroes battling the establishment, but may be the representatives of their Houses, interest groups, etc, who may want you in power because it suits their own interests.<br /> <br /> For example, in the Dragonblood game I used to play, a retired PC had become Empress, and promptly gone into seclusion so as to not be assassinated.<br /> Thus, real power was wielded by her consort, Hearth-mates, etc, most of which were from House Pelleps.<br /> <br /> So, when our PCs overthrew the Prime Minister and replaced him as representatives of the Empress's will, it wasn't really just us vs him, it was House Cathak/Sesus/Mnemon/Ledaal/Tepet/Cynis/the All-Seeing Eye/the Sidereals/the liberal wing of the Immaculate Order/some Lunars who wanted to make peace with the Realm vs House Pelleps/the conservative faction of the Immaculate Order.<br /> <br /> Dynastic games are very much about family, and that means your PC isn't necessarily fighting alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T07:25:42-07:00","id":1228574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1227771-can-a-circle-of-dynasts-win?p=1228236#post1228236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was what I was getting at. It's not that Solars are bad at social-fu, they're very good at it.<br /> But often having such power makes it too tempting not to co-operate with people, but instead bulldoze them with social-fu (or kung-fu).</div> </div> </div> </div>One of my favourite ways of trolling players is having the occasional NPC spend willpower but still go along with what the PCs want in the short-term especially if they're being confronted with caste marks, drawn daiklaves and flared animas.<br /> <br /> Sometimes there's betrayal later down the line, other times there's a moment over tea years later on when the eventually won over NPC admits that they spent months dancing on eggshells while dealing with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T11:03:06-07:00","id":1228628,"title":"","content":"Ah yes, that has definitely happened with my players.<br /> <br /> Once they seized power over a kingdom basically through intimidation. The other local kings told them they accepted the PC's puppet king... then secretly called in the Wyld Hunt (which of course, led to the PCs killing most of the local kings).<br /> <br /> Another time they took control of the 4 Djala Kingdoms by controlling its religion. The King of the Southern Djala sucked up to them, tried to manipulate them against each other, used them to take down his enemies, and then called in the Sidereals to break their control.<br /> Unfortunately, he then decided he was politically powerful enoughto exile one of the PCs for his blatant interference in Djala politics... who came back and killed him.<br /> <br /> Essence 5 Celestials don't really compromise much.*<br /> <br /> <br /> *It's probably worth adding that the same players seem, in my experience, to compromise and negotiate a lot more when playing weaker characters like DBs, in case anyone thinks this is just a matter of the players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T08:09:38-07:00","id":1228858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1227771-can-a-circle-of-dynasts-win?p=1228133#post1228133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not just social stuff, if you took a group of chargen DBs and pitted them up against Octavian, Siggereth and a legion of 500 blood apes, there's almost no way to win. Barring maybe some weird exploity white room thing like everyone taking 3 5-dot command merits and just drowning them in legions or something. Which isn't to say that the cause is hopeless either, you're just going to need some way to maybe separate them, like discover that Octavian has an ancient geas put on him by some anathema that prevents him from turning down an invitation to a summer fire festival or something. Or perhaps find some hellish intrigue that you can use to pit them against each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an aside, while i know what you meant, this ended up being an unintentionally hilarious example, as Octavian and Sigereth are as diametrically opposite to each other as any pair of stated beings can be.<br /> <br /> Just <b>look</b> at their Intimacies, really.<br /> <br /> Honestly the only thing a prospective hero - damn, even a mortal one might be more than enough - would need to do to deal with them is catch on to that amd point out someone got them on the same side.<br /> <br /> ...and get the hell away very quickly indeed, if you want to live to tell this tale one day. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-20-2018, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}